   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:75d3a172-f88d-4ef1-85ad-1c4a45ad0f97",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c5db0a47d1b953fb365572bcefb156ed?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSP-3.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c5db0a47d1b953fb365572bcefb156ed?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSP-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c5db0a47d1b953fb365572bcefb156ed?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSP-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c5db0a47d1b953fb365572bcefb156ed?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSP-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Scott Prater",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A75d3a172-f88d-4ef1-85ad-1c4a45ad0f97",
      "timeZone": "America/Chicago"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I looked more into this, and I realized that creating an index for a single datastream in a way that does not index all datastreams is not a trivial task, given that the filesystem layout for any particular Fedora instance can vary:  it can be legacy or Akubra, and within Akubra, it can be split into any combination of n-tuples, with varying depths.  In short, in order to calculate the filesystem path for a datastream object in Fedora, we need to know what storage provider Fedora is using, and how it is configured – which means reading and interpreting the Fedora configuration itself.  To do this, we would need to introduce a dependency on the Fedora configurations, as well as duplicate path calculation algorithms implemented in the Fedora and Akubra codebase.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "This strikes me as an unacceptable approach.  I recommend closing this ticket as \"Won't fix\", and recommending that organizations with large repositories create the datastream index once, then re-use it.  ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Unfortunately, every time there is a change to their repository, their datastream index will need to be wiped and recreated; perhaps there might be a less onerous approach to updating an existing datastream index (but that's another ticket).",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
